      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62193d56b67a676d221e2458",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've discovered a temporary workaround! :D\nThe problem is definitely the OVRPlugin.dll file itself, as something is wrong with the version of this file currently being distributed with VRChat. I tried replacing the OVRPlugin.dll for VRChat with the OVRPlugin.dll from a different Oculus app which I knew was working fine and VRChat properly boots into VR now! That said, different games are going to have different builds of the OVRPlugin.dll file so I don't think this is guaranteed to work and is going to depend on which game you try to pull this file from. The game I pulled my replacement from is Master Bladesmith, as I knew it was updated very recently and thus would have a recent build of that file.\nI should also note I have now tested both the Live and OpenBeta builds on Oculus and BOTH are suffering from this issue, so for those of you working on VRChat, please get that OVRPlugin.dll file fixed up!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
