      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62193d56b67a676d221e2458",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "EXTREMELY IMPORTANT FOR VRCHAT DEVS: Update to latest build of Oculus Integration SDK for Unity ASAP!! That may be all it takes to fix this issue we've been having!\nMore Details:\nI've been doing some research and apparently, the problem all of us are having may be related to an issue which cropped up in the previous release of the Oculus Integration SDK for Unity, specifically with CPUs which do not support AVX2 instructions. (I have an AMD FX-8350 which, AFAIK, does not have AVX2 instructions support.)\nThe latest build as of the day I'm writing this (which will result in an OVRPlugin version of 1.70, VRChat is currently using 1.69) indicates that this specific issue has been fixed. I don't code with Unity so do not have an easy way to test this out; if anyone here does, please try this out and see what happens when dropping in the 1.70 version of the DLL into VRChat!\nGonna send another eMail to the VRChat team ASAP to let them know about this too!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
