      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "62193d56b67a676d221e2458",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "According to Wikipedia, among Intel processors, the first to ship with AVX2 were Haswell Core and Xeon CPUs in 2013. followed by Haswell-E and Broadwell in 2014.  \nMy CPU (which I've previously noted is an i7-3820) is a Sandy Bridge-E from 2012, predating AVX2, so it sounds like this could very well be the smoking gun.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
